well sharks beachgoers worst nightmare  of course so far in North Carolina there  have been eight shark attacks in just  under a month but at the Discovery  Network sharks are the stars of shark  week this week we spoke to andy  casagrande cinematographer of shark week  about the perils of shooting these  sharp-toothed creatures for me like the  two coolest things about my job are the  Sharks and the cameras and all the  technology involved so you know  especially with you know little cameras  like GoPros you can put them essentially  anywhere so that's really like  revolutionized how we can capture  different shots we put a GoPro on the  fin of a great white shark at the  Neptune Islands and that shark actually  swim around and filmed this other shark  Joan it was there's a pretty sketchy  moment where I'm trying to put the GoPro  on the fin and I kind of fall in the  water and you know cut to commercial it  was you'll have to watch to see what I  mean the reality is the Predators still  hunt the same way they always have for  millions of years the only thing that's  changing is the technology that we can  use to capture you know new insights  into their behavior and the fact that  essentially anyone now can go out and  grab their camera a GoPro or whatever  they want and go out and film their own  shark week to be I kind of feel like a  cinema scientist so everything from like  infrared cameras thermal cameras as i  mentioned drones to me are amazing i  captured some really nice great white  sharks breaching on my drone super high  resolution cameras like the red epic  shoots 6k resolution i also have a  phantom flex which shoots a thousand  frames per second at 4k so you can slow  down you know the bite of a shark or the  jump or the breach to like you know 52  you know a hundred times slower than the  speed of life it's not only mind-blowing  to watch it's actually helping  scientists learn more about the  predators and it's exciting it's fun I  think it's a great union between science  and cinema and shark week lets me do all  of that
 

